From eae89ff4541c03d75bedeaf5637f6910c733ee62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hecheng Yu <kde-yyds@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:13:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] dodge: Clamp 720p capture rate to 30fps to fix 7.5fps
 recording

The 4x-slow-motion problem of the 8K fix applies to 720p as well: after
switching 4K120 -> 720p, CommonVideoMode.li() returns 120.0 (stale fps
state) and MediaRecorder.setCaptureRate(120) is sent while the encoder
outputs 30fps, producing a file that plays at 7.5fps (120/30).

Extend the li() clamp so it also returns 30.0 when the video size is 720p:

  com/oplus/camera/module/a.li()  if G6() == "video_size_8k"  return 30.0
                                  if G6() == "video_size_720p" return 30.0

With this, 720p30 records at the correct 30fps cadence. 1080p120/4K120
still bypass the clamp. Only required on OxygenOS 16.0.8.301 and later,
where the native encoder honors the time-lapse capture rate.
---
 smali_classes12/com/oplus/camera/module/a.smali | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes12/com/oplus/camera/module/a.smali b/smali_classes12/com/oplus/camera/module/a.smali
index 6c7d960..2e49da8 100644
--- a/smali_classes12/com/oplus/camera/module/a.smali
+++ b/smali_classes12/com/oplus/camera/module/a.smali
@@ -30112,10 +30112,19 @@
 
     invoke-virtual {v0, v1}, Ljava/lang/String;->equals(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z
 
-    move-result v0
+    move-result v1
+
+    if-nez v1, :cond_30fps
+
+    const-string v1, "video_size_720p"
+
+    invoke-virtual {v0, v1}, Ljava/lang/String;->equals(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z
+
+    move-result v1
 
-    if-eqz v0, :cond_8k
+    if-eqz v1, :cond_8k
 
+    :cond_30fps
     const-wide/high16 v0, 0x403e000000000000L    # 30.0
 
     invoke-static {v0, v1}, Ljava/lang/Double;->valueOf(D)Ljava/lang/Double;
